k><name>YOSHIDA MOTOHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOITA, MASAO</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAYAMA, KATSUYA</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SUMITOMO ELECTRIC INDUSTRIES, LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, MOTOHIDE</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOITA MASAO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NAGAYAMA KATSUYA</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA MOTOHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOITA, MASAO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NAGAYAMA, KATSUYA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>YOSHIDA, MOTOHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A method for producing an optical fiber having a low polarization dispersion characteristic achieved by suitable twisting the optical fiber even the optical fiber is produced at a fiber drawing speed of over 250 m/min and having a small variation in diameter and a small variation in the outside diameter in the length direction.  The method comprising softening an optical fiber matrix by heating, drawing an optical fiber (11) downward from the matrix, covering the optical fiber (11) with a coating, axially twisting the optical fiber by means of a rocking guide roller (13) which periodically rocks is characterized in that the rocking amplitude at the roller face (13a) of the rocking guide roller (13) where the optical fiber (11) comes into contact first is in a range between +/-7 mm and +/-0.5 mm in a direction perpendicular to the vertical.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>Procédé permettant de produire une fibre optique qui possède une caractéristique de dispersion de polarisation faible, obtenue par la torsion appropriée de ladite fibre alors même que celle-ci est produite à une vitesse d'étirement supérieure à 250 m/min, et qui présente de faibles variations de diamètre et de diamètre extérieur en direction longitudinale. Selon le procédé, on ramollit par chauffage une matrice de fibre optique, on étire une fibre optique (11) vers le bas depuis ladite matrice, on recouvre la fibre avec un revêtement et on la tord axialement au moyen d'un rouleau de guidage oscillant (13) à oscillation périodique. Le procédé est caractérisé par le fait que l'amplitude d'oscillation, au niveau de la face (13a) du rouleau oscillant (13) avec laquelle la fibre entre d'abord en contact, est comprise entre +/- 7 mm et +/- 0,5 mm dans une direction perpendiculaire à la verticale.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>